MONOCHROME INTER AT NON-8-ALIGNED SIZES — defect fix measurement.
The DPB reference kept the coded pad columns where every conforming
decoder edge-extends the SIGNALLED frame edge (C pad_input_picture inside
pad_ref_and_set_flags, enc_dec_process.c:1088). pad_ref_visible_edge now
replicates the visible edge across the non-visible columns/rows on the u8
recon and the 10-bit canvas before the reference margin is generated.

date:   2026-09-25
host:   i265 (x86_64 Linux 7.0.0-34-generic)
cmd:    SVTAV1_MONO=1 SVTAV1_FRAMES=3 SVTAV1_INTRA_PERIOD=64 \
        SVTAV1_HIER_LEVELS=0 SVTAV1_INTERDBG=1 SVTAV1_FINAL_RECON=rec \
        SVTAV1_FRAME_SHIFT=13 \
        target/release/examples/identity_run <content> w h 40 7 p
        then aomdec --rawvideo + dav1d on p.obu, byte-compare each frame
        (under run-heavy --mem 8G --jobs 6)

